  "summary": "Monday 10/26 St. Brigid CT list prepared per RBC-RAD-07. Four booked studies (appt-00001, -00006, -00008 cancelled; not ordered).\n\n1) pt-0047 Mohr, 08:00 CT A/P w/ contrast (sr-t0001). No contrast reaction; diet-controlled T2DM; last Cr 09/24 >30 days -> pre-scan creatinine ordered (sr-t0009). New outside Cr 1.52 (10/22) arrived mid-work: eGFR ~64, not AKI by policy definition (prior value 28 days earlier) -> protocol decision unchanged; pre-scan creatinine kept. Patient instructed (comm-t0011) + update (comm-t0026); follow-up task t0032.\n\n2) pt-0015 Ferreira, 09:00 CT A/P w/ contrast (sr-t0002). 2019 iohexol reaction graded MODERATE by the radiology report of the day (allergy-list \"anaphylaxis, patient report\" does not change grade) -> §2 prednisone 50 mg 20:00/02:00/08:00 (mr-t0005) + diphenhydramine 50 mg 08:00 (mr-t0006), needs driver. Creatinine 10/14 was CORRECTED to 2.8 (eGFR ~24) -> added NaCl 0.9% 500 mL IV at 08:00 (mr-t0020); corrected Spanish/English instructions sent (comm-t0012, correction comm-t0024); clinical follow-up task t0031.\n\n3) pt-0049 Schuster, 13:00 CT A/P w/ contrast (sr-t0003). AKI 10/04 ED (Cr 1.52, not back to baseline) -> pre-scan creatinine (sr-t0010), NaCl 0.9% 500 mL IV at 12:00 (mr-t0007), metformin mr-00392 on hold (>=48 h post-scan, restart only after normal recheck; task t0015). Outside report arriving mid-work showed moderate iopamidol reaction 2022 -> added prednisone 50 mg 00:00/06:00/12:00 (mr-t0021) + diphenhydramine 50 mg 12:00 (mr-t0022), needs driver. Instructions comm-t0013, updated comm-t0025; allergy-list task t0033 (no iopamidol code in catalog).\n\n4) pt-0046 Beahan, 14:00 CT A/P without contrast (sr-t0004) ordered as booked; patient told no prep needed (comm-t0014). Outside report of a prior mild iohexol reaction recorded on allergy list (alg-t0023); no change since the study is non-contrast.\n\nNotes and addenda written for each patient citing RBC-RAD-07; the four new inbox items closed with links. Older inbox items for other patients weren't touched.",
